 "l10.31f96331": "Principle",
 "l10.404d5bef": "thought-long",
 "l10.475c4209": "Create your own words",
 "l10.481e4a14": "\"Bicycle\" → `mana-puta` (round-foot)",
 "l10.55779eb1": "Translate into Tapi, using compounds:",
 "l10.56603e6d": "know-give = teacher",
 "l10.63f40b36": "Classic examples:",
 "l10.6b25bffe": "\"Airport\" → `kama-titu-kama` (airplane-house)",
 "l10.732b452c": "Example: \"saudade\" (longing) has no direct word. Possible compounds:",
 "l10.736875cf": "Final exercise",
 "l10.acaedb0a": "heart-return",
 "l10.b2e8f164": "time-negation",
 "l10.d426691e": "Lesson 10 — Compounding (the soul of Tapi)",
 "l10.df5dd4a7": "word-long = telephone",
 "l10.f5e910db": "\"Happiness\" → `pumu-tina`",
 "l10.f78934c9": "Combine roots to form concepts. Speakers understand from context.",
 "l11.10fef620": "English",
 "l11.18b7aedc": "\"The rain will make the plant grow\" → `masu patuka kipi tipi`",
 "l11.19b624e9": "\"you will make the child sleep\"",
 "l11.319ac7ae": "Causative = \"make X happen\". In Tapi: `patu` (make/do) + verb.",
 "l11.3d3cd5cd": "Tense goes on the verb `patu`, not on the main verb:",
 "l11.46dc33ac": "\"mother makes the child sleep\"",
 "l11.4a55b475": "Vocabulary",
 "l11.5153cd83": "Lesson 11 — Causative",
 "l11.67528e5a": "to force (lit. must-make)",
 "l11.7ddc9575": "\"They made me laugh\" → `kupi patuta mi tasi`",
 "l11.83d76e7f": "\"teacher makes person know\" (= teaches)",
 "l11.968db0cb": "to kill (= patu kina, but a short root)",
 "l11.b3884c47": "\"I made him eat (yesterday)\"",
 "l11.bd3e0f5f": "to make (causative)",
 "l11.c87c951b": "\"I made him eat\"",
 "l11.cfd1e384": "Tapi",
 "l11.e5b8d17b": "Structure",
 "l11.e87b32ab": "`SUBJ + patu + TARGET + VERB`.",
 "l11.f3cf4433": "Exercises",
 "l12.04f3381b": "Active: `si mani kasi` = \"he eats the food\"",
 "l12.0f1d861c": "\"the book was written by many people\"",
 "l12.12a28a47": "Passive: `kasi mani-pa mu si` = \"the food is eaten by him\"",
 "l12.2a3586b5": "\"the food was eaten by him\"",
 "l12.50f62116": "`OBJECT + VERB + mu + AGENT`.",
 "l12.5e59093b": "\"Suanu was seen by the mother\" → `Suanu tikata mu mama`",
 "l12.ac4fb66f": "Without `mu`: impersonal passive.",
 "l12.af87cd2c": "Lesson 12 — Passive voice",
 "l12.c350c950": "\"the house was built\" (by someone unstated)",
 "l12.c9595b8f": "Swaps subject and object. The particle `mu` marks the agent.",
 "l12.d75644fe": "\"The tree was cut down\" → `tipa sasita`",
 "l12.d78a1d07": "Unknown agent",
 "l12.e5b8d17b": "Structure",
 "l12.f3cf4433": "Exercises",
 "l12.fbbc5ba4": "Compare:",
 "l13.0ba520d3": "`manita-ni` (must have eaten — I saw the dirty dishes)",
 "l13.0e23e5c5": "∅ (nothing)",
 "l13.10fef620": "English",
 "l13.12efe565": "When to use",
 "l13.226ed3c2": "\"I saw that he slept\" → `napita`",
 "l13.30f97a51": "Example",
 "l13.3107f050": "to see (root of direct evidence)",
 "l13.34c4a1b8": "I inferred from evidence",
 "l13.46e18882": "Suffix",
 "l13.4a55b475": "Vocabulary",
 "l13.4dc85172": "Rumor: `-ni-ku` (doubtful)",
 "l13.4fe4525a": "`manita` (he ate, I saw it)",
 "l13.60694dcc": "\"Maybe he came\" → `unata-ni-ku`",
